Endpoint: GET /chat/completions
- OperationId: listChatCompletions
- Tag: Chat
- Summary: List Chat Completions
- Query parameters:
  - model (string, optional): model used to generate chat completions
  - metadata (object|null, optional): up to 16 key-value pairs for filtering results; keys max 64 chars, values max 512 chars. Query format example: metadata[key1]=value1&metadata[key2]=value2
  - after (string, optional): cursor ID for pagination (last completion from previous request)
  - limit (integer, optional, default 20): number of chat completions to retrieve
  - order (string, optional, default asc): asc|desc by timestamp
- 200 Response (application/json): ChatCompletionList
  - object: "list"
  - data: array of ChatCompletion objects

ChatCompletion object (represents a chat completion response)
- id (string)
- created (integer): Unix timestamp (seconds)
- model (string): model used
- service_tier (string|null, default auto): auto|default|flex|scale|priority
  - Controls processing tier. auto uses project setting (default is default unless configured). default is standard pricing/performance. flex/priority are special tiers. Response includes the actual tier used; may differ from requested.
- system_fingerprint (string, deprecated): identifies backend configuration; can be used with seed to understand backend changes
- choices (array of Choice)
  - Required: finish_reason, index, message, logprobs
  - finish_reason (string): stop | length | tool_calls | content_filter | function_call (deprecated)
  - index (integer): index in choices
  - message (AssistantMessage)
    - role: "assistant"
    - content: string|null
    - refusal: string|null
    - tool_calls (array): tool calls generated by the model; discriminator: type
      - Function tool call:
        - id (string)
        - type: "function"
        - function: { name (string), arguments (string JSON) }
          - Note: JSON may be invalid or include hallucinated params; validate before calling
      - Custom tool call:
        - id (string)
        - type: "custom"
        - custom: { name (string), input (string) }
    - annotations (array): URL citations when using web search
      - items:
        - type: "url_citation"
        - url_citation: { start_index (int), end_index (int), url (string), title (string) }
    - function_call (object, deprecated): { name (string), arguments (string JSON) } replaced by tool_calls
    - audio (object|null): present if audio modality requested
      - id (string): unique audio response ID
      - expires_at (integer): Unix timestamp when audio is no longer accessible for multi-turn use
      - data (string): base64-encoded audio bytes in requested format
      - transcript (string): transcript of generated audio
    - Required fields on message: role, content, refusal
  - logprobs (object|null): log probability info for the choice
    - content (array|null of TokenWithLogprobs)
    - refusal (array|null of TokenWithLogprobs)
    - TokenWithLogprobs:
      - token (string)
      - logprob (number): -9999.0 indicates very unlikely (outside top 20)
      - bytes (array<int>|null): UTF-8 bytes for the token (useful for multi-token chars)
      - top_logprobs (array): most likely tokens at this position; items contain token, logprob, bytes

Notes
- The list response’s top-level object is always "list" and contains an array of chat completion objects.
- Ordering in list endpoint is by timestamp; default ascending unless order=desc is specified.
Tool `OpenAPI Explorer:getApiOperation` with Parameter {'id': 'openai', 'operationIdOrRoute': '/completions'} on OpenAPI Explorer succeeded. Result (summarized from 24857 tokens): OpenAPI overview
- Version: 3.1.0; API title: OpenAI API (version 2.3.0)
- Description: OpenAI REST API (see https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference)
- Terms: https://openai.com/policies/terms-of-use
- Contact: OpenAI Support (https://help.openai.com/)
- License: MIT (https://github.com/openai/openai-openapi/blob/master/LICENSE)
- Server: https://api.openai.com/v1
- Security: ApiKeyAuth (use Authorization: Bearer <API key>)

Endpoint
- POST /completions — Create completion (legacy: Completions API; streamed and non-streamed responses share the same shape, unlike chat)
- Required request body fields: model, prompt

Request body (application/json)
- model (string)
  - ID of the model to use; see Models list/overview
  - Preset enum noted: gpt-3.5-turbo-instruct, davinci-002, babbage-002
- prompt (string or array)
  - May be: string; array of strings; array of tokens (integers); array of token arrays
  - Nullable; default '' for string forms
  - Note: <|endoftext|> is the document separator used in training; if no prompt, model generates from a new document start
- best_of (integer, 0–20; default 1; nullable)
  - Generates best_of completions server-side and returns the best (highest logprob/token); results cannot be streamed
  - When used with n, best_of controls candidates and must be > n
  - Can quickly consume tokens; tune max_tokens and stop
- echo (boolean; default false; nullable): Echo back prompt in addition to completion
- frequency_penalty (number, -2 to 2; default 0; nullable): Penalizes tokens based on existing frequency to reduce repetition
- presence_penalty (number, -2 to 2; default 0; nullable): Penalizes tokens if they appear so far, encouraging new topics
- logit_bias (object map token_id -> int; nullable)
  - Values -100 to 100; added to logits; small magnitudes slightly change likelihood; ±100 can effectively ban/force tokens
  - Example: {"50256": -100} prevents <|endoftext|>
- logprobs (integer 0–5; default null; nullable): Include logprobs for up to N most likely tokens plus the chosen token
- max_tokens (integer ≥0; default 16; nullable): Max tokens to generate; prompt tokens + max_tokens ≤ model context length
- n (integer 1–128; default 1; nullable): Number of completions to generate per prompt; may consume quota quickly
- seed (int64; nullable): Best-effort determinism; pair with system_fingerprint in response to monitor backend changes; not guaranteed
- stop (string or array of up to 4 strings; nullable)
  - Not supported with latest reasoning models o3 and o4-mini
  - Up to 4 stop sequences; returned text omits the stop sequence
  - String default shown as <|endoftext|>
- stream (boolean; default false; nullable)
  - If true, tokens stream as server-sent events; stream ends with data: [DONE]
- stream_options (object or null)
  - Only set when stream: true
  - include_usage (boolean): If true, an additional usage chunk is sent before [DONE] with total token usage; other chunks include usage: null; if stream is interrupted, final usage chunk may be missing
  - include_obfuscation (boolean): When true, enable stream obfuscation (adds random characters in an obfuscation field to normalize payload sizes). Obfuscation fields are included by default; set false to optimize bandwidth if network is trusted
- suffix (string; nullable; default null): Suffix after inserted text completion; only supported for gpt-3.5-turbo-instruct
- temperature (number 0–2; default 1; nullable): Higher is more random; typically adjust temperature or top_p, not both
- top_p (number 0–1; default 1; nullable): Nucleus sampling; typically adjust top_p or temperature, not both
- user (string): End-user identifier for abuse monitoring

Response (200 application/json)
- Object: text_completion
- Required fields: id (string), object ("text_completion"), created (unix seconds, int), model (string), choices (array)
- Optional: system_fingerprint (string): Backend configuration fingerprint (use with seed to assess determinism changes
