      - description (string, optional): describes what the function does
      - parameters (object, optional): JSON Schema for function args; omit to define empty parameter list
      - strict (boolean|null, default false): when true, model adheres strictly to provided JSON Schema (subset supported; see Structured Outputs guide)
  - Note: tools use discriminator property "type"
- tool_resources (object|null): resources for tools
  - code_interpreter:
    - file_ids (array of strings, max 20; default []): file IDs available to code interpreter
  - file_search:
    - vector_store_ids (array of strings, max 1): attached vector store IDs
- metadata (object|null): up to 16 key-value pairs
  - Keys: strings max 64 chars; Values: strings max 512 chars
- temperature (number|null): 0–2; default 1
  - Higher = more random, lower = more deterministic
- top_p (number|null): 0–1; default 1
  - Nucleus sampling alternative to temperature; generally adjust one, not both
- response_format (one of | null): controls output format
  - "auto" (string): default
  - Text object:
    - type: "text" (default behavior for text responses)
  - JSON object:
    - type: "json_object" (older JSON mode)
    - Note: model will not produce JSON without explicit instruction in system/user messages
  - JSON schema:
    - type: "json_schema"
    - json_schema:
      - name (string) [required]: a-z, A-Z, 0–9, underscores, dashes; max 64
      - description (string, optional): what the format is for
      - schema (object): JSON Schema describing response
      - strict (boolean|null, default false): when true, model strictly follows provided schema (subset supported; see Structured Outputs)
  - Important JSON mode notes (from docs):
    - When using JSON mode, you must instruct the model to output JSON; otherwise it may stream whitespace until limits are reached
