Path: PATCH /user (users/update-authenticated)
- Summary: Update the authenticated user
- Description: If your email is private and you send an email in the update, privacy settings still hide it from public profile/API.
- Tags: users
- Docs: https://docs.github.com/rest/users/users#update-the-authenticated-user
- Request body (application/json, optional) fields:
  - name (string), email (string), blog (string), twitter_username (string, nullable), company (string), location (string), hireable (boolean), bio (string)
  - Example: update blog and name
- Responses:
  - 200 application/json: Private User schema (as in GET)
  - 304: Not modified
  - 401: Requires authentication (Basic Error)
  - 403: Forbidden (Basic Error)
  - 404: Resource not found (Basic Error)
  - 422: Validation failed or spammed endpoint (Validation Error schema):
    - Required: message, documentation_url
    - Optional errors[] items: { resource, field, message, code (required), index, value (string|integer|array, nullable) }
- x-github: githubCloudOnly=false; enabledForGitHubApps=false; category=subcategory: users

Schemas referenced in errors
- Basic Error: { message: string, documentation_url: string, url: string, status: string }
- Validation Error: { message, documentation_url, errors[] with detailed fields as above }

