Endpoint: POST /responses
- OperationId: createResponse
- Tag: Responses
- Summary: Create a model response
- Request body: application/json (required)

Key request fields (combined via allOf)
- metadata: object | null
  - Up to 16 key-value pairs. Keys: strings ≤64 chars; values: strings ≤512 chars. Useful for storing/querying extra info.
- top_logprobs: integer [0, 20] | null
  - Returns N most likely tokens with log probabilities at each position.
- temperature: number [0, 2] | null (default 1)
  - Higher = more random; lower = more deterministic. Adjust temperature or top_p, not both.
- top_p: number [0, 1] | null (default 1)
  - Nucleus sampling; considers tokens within top_p probability mass. Adjust this or temperature, not both.
- user: string (deprecated)
  - Replaced by safety_identifier and prompt_cache_key. Previously used for cache bucketing and abuse detection.
- safety_identifier: string
  - Stable per-end-user identifier for safety/abuse detection. Recommend hashing usernames/emails. See safety best practices.
- prompt_cache_key: string
  - Stable key to optimize prompt caching; replaces user. See prompt caching guide.
- service_tier: enum | null (default auto)
  - Values: auto, default, flex, scale, priority.
  - Controls processing/pricing tier. If set, the response includes the actual service_tier used, which may differ from the requested value. See tier docs; flex/priority described in linked guides.
- prompt_cache_retention: enum | null
  - Values: in-memory, 24h. Set 24h for extended prompt caching up to 24 hours.

Conversation and model
- previous_response_id: string | null
  - Link to a prior response to create multi-turn conversations. Cannot be used with conversation.
- model: string
