  - object: "list"
  - data: array of certificate objects; each item represents a certificate and includes:
    - object (string; enum):
      - "certificate": when creating, updating, or getting a specific certificate.
      - "organization.certificate": when listing/activating/deactivating at org level.
      - "organization.project.certificate": when listing/activating/deactivating at project level.
    - id (string): identifier for API references.
    - name (string): certificate name.
    - created_at (integer): Unix timestamp (seconds) when uploaded.
    - certificate_details (object):
      - valid_at (integer): Unix timestamp (seconds) when certificate becomes valid.
      - expires_at (integer): Unix timestamp (seconds) when certificate expires.
      - content (string): PEM-encoded certificate content. (Note: examples may omit content in list context.)
    - active (boolean): whether the certificate is currently active at the scope of the listing. Not returned when retrieving a specific certificate.
  - Pagination:
    - first_id (string)
    - last_id (string)
    - has_more (boolean)
  - Required fields (per item): object, id, name, created_at, certificate_details
- Example usage (from metadata):
  - Request (curl): GET https://api.openai.com/v1/organization/certificates with Authorization: Bearer $OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY
  - Response example (abbrev): object "list"; data includes items with object "organization.certificate", id "cert_abc", name, active true, created_at, certificate_details (valid_at, expires_at); has_more false.

