- Mean-field Modelling of Moiré Materials: A User's Guide with Selected Applications to Twisted Bilayer Graphene (arXiv:2511.21683v1)
  - Authors: Yves H. Kwan; Ziwei Wang; Glenn Wagner; Nick Bultinck; Steven H. Simon; Siddharth A. Parameswaran
  - Scope: Tutorial review on continuum modelling and Hartree-Fock (HF) mean-field for magic-angle TBG, including ground states and collective excitations.
  - Case studies: (1) Chiral-flat strong-coupling limit and its limitations; (2) Intermediate-coupling incommensurate Kekulé spiral (IKS) induced by heterostrain; (3) hBN-aligned orbital Chern insulators and domain wall energetics in translationally non-invariant settings.
  - Provides open-source code guidance for modelling.
  - Links: pdf https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.21683v1

- On Evolution-Based Models for Experimentation Under Interference (arXiv:2511.21675v1)
  - Authors: Sadegh Shirani; Mohsen Bayati
  - Thesis: For population-level causal effects under interference, exact network recovery is unnecessary; instead, model outcome evolution across rounds under interventions.
  - Contributions: Axiomatic conditions for low-dimensional recursive “evolution mappings” of outcome distributions; a distributional analogue of difference-in-differences exploiting parallel evolution across treatments; shows randomization implicitly samples hidden spillover channels, enabling learning of heterogeneous spillovers.
  - Instantiations/limits: Causal message passing in dense networks; influencer networks; challenges with strong temporal trends or endogenous interference.
  - Links: pdf https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.21675v1

- On the generalized Keffer form of the Dzyaloshinskii constant: its consequences for the spin, momentum and polarization evolution (arXiv:2511.21672v1)
  - Author: Pavel A. Andreev
  - Content: Reviews three microscopic contributions to the Dzyaloshinskii-Moriya interaction (DMI) constant and combines them into a generalized Keffer form. Proposes further generalizations and analyzes macroscopic consequences in Landau–Lifshitz–Gilbert dynamics, momentum balance, and polarization evolution.
  - Also suggests an analogue of the Keffer form for the symmetric Heisenberg exchange integral highlighting ligand contributions.
  - Links: pdf https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.21672v1

