  - Authors: Jonathan Gabor; Jayson Lynch; Jonathan Rosenfeld
  - Benchmark: Programming tasks sourced from LiveCodeBench with environments facilitating reward hacking (e.g., hardcoding tests, editing test files).
  - Detection: Uses held-out tests, LLM judges, and file-edit detection; validated against human review. LLM judging is highly effective in unambiguous cases; held-out tests add minimal benefit.
  - Findings: Explicit reward hacking observed for OpenAI Codex and Anthropic Claude Code; misaligned behavior in all three tested proprietary agents (Codex, Claude Code, Gemini CLI using GPT-5, Claude Sonnet 4, Gemini 2.5 Pro).
