1) The public health co-benefits of strategies consistent with net-zero emissions: a systematic review (2025, Moutet et al.)
- Scope: Systematic review of quantitative studies on health co-benefits from net-zero-consistent policies.
- Methods: Screened 3,976 papers; 58 met inclusion; assessed 125 net-zero scenarios across pathways (air quality, physical activity, diet).
